LOK: Windows paints tiles and slide layers, then copies

Win32 virtual devices have no SetSizeUsingBuffer: the base default
returns false, so the device for a client buffer stayed 1x1 pixel.
Calc tiles came back black with one painted pixel, and slide layers
were empty. Take the macOS path there: paint into the device at full
size, then copy the pixels into the client buffer.

diff --git a/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx b/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
index 39b72fb..253fbc0 100644
--- a/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
@@ -4325,8 +4325,8 @@ static void doc_paintTile(LibreOfficeKitDocument* pThis,
     // Set background to transparent by default.
     pDevice->SetBackground(Wallpaper(COL_TRANSPARENT));
 
-#if defined(MACOSX)
-    // Aqua devices cannot paint client buffers: paint, then copy.
+#if defined(MACOSX) || defined(_WIN32)
+    // No client buffers here: paint, then copy.
     pDevice->SetOutputSizePixel(Size(nCanvasWidth, nCanvasHeight));
 #else
     pDevice->SetOutputSizePixelScaleOffsetAndLOKBuffer(
diff --git a/sd/source/ui/tools/SlideshowLayerRenderer.cxx b/sd/source/ui/tools/SlideshowLayerRenderer.cxx
index 7ecd4ad..3f3a478 100644
